# Implementation Plan - HOTFIX-011B — Fix Global Focus Shortcut Using Ctrl+Alt+E

Replace global focus shortcut `Ctrl+E` with `Ctrl + Alt + E` (`MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT` + `VK_E`) and fix the Win64 `MSG` ctypes structure alignment so `wParam` reads correctly at offset 16.

## Proposed Changes

### Platform Layer

#### [MODIFY] [global_hotkey.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/platform/global_hotkey.py)
- Correct `MSG` structure field types for Win64 ABI:
  - `hwnd`: `c_void_p` (8 bytes)
  - `message`: `c_uint` (4 bytes)
  - `wParam`: `c_ulonglong` (8 bytes, `UINT_PTR`/`WPARAM`, byte offset 16)
  - `lParam`: `c_longlong` (8 bytes, `LONG_PTR`/`LPARAM`, byte offset 24)
- Define `MOD_ALT = 0x0001` and `HOTKEY_ID_CTRL_ALT_E = 0x011C`.
- Update `WindowsGlobalHotkeyManager` to handle `Ctrl+Alt+E` registration with `MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT`.

#### [MODIFY] [__init__.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/platform/__init__.py)
- Export `MOD_ALT` and `HOTKEY_ID_CTRL_ALT_E`.

---

### UI & Main Window Layer

#### [MODIFY] [overlay_visibility_panel.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/overlay_visibility_panel.py)
- Update hint label: `"Shortcuts: Ctrl+Q decrease opacity · Ctrl+W increase opacity · Ctrl+Alt+E focus"`.

#### [MODIFY] [main_window.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/main_window.py)
- Register `Ctrl + Alt + E` (`MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT`, `VK_E`, `HOTKEY_ID_CTRL_ALT_E`).
- In `nativeEvent`, match `msg.message == WM_HOTKEY` and `msg.wParam == HOTKEY_ID_CTRL_ALT_E` using the corrected 64-bit `MSG` structure layout.
- Call `restore_and_focus()` on `WM_HOTKEY` match, preserving current transparency level and settings intact.

